    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15824" root="رطن" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا رُطَيْنَاكَ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُطَّيْنَاكَ</span> means <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا الذَّى تَرْطُنُ بِهِ</span>
[i. e. <i>What is that to which thou alludest, not
mentioning it explicitly?</i>]: (JM:) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا رُطَّيْنَاكَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذِهِ</span>, and sometimes without teshdeed, means
<i>What is</i> [<i>this</i>] <i>thy speech?</i> (K.)

